cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use the Digital Legacy Protocol specification, reference
  implementation, or accompanying whitepaper in academic work, please
  cite both the software and the whitepaper as indicated below.
title: "Digital Legacy Protocol: A Quorum-Based Framework for Verifiable Digital Inheritance"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Ciprian Ștefan
    family-names: Pleșca
    alias: Stefano
    affiliation: Independent Researcher
repository-code: "https://github.com/Ciprian-LocalPulse/digital-legacy-protocol"
url: "https://github.com/Ciprian-LocalPulse/digital-legacy-protocol"
abstract: >-
  An open specification and reference implementation for verifiable
  digital inheritance, addressing the absence of a consistent standard
  for the disposition of digital assets after death or incapacitation.
  The protocol verifies incapacitation via a trustee quorum rather than
  unilateral platform determination, splits protected secrets via
  Shamir's Secret Sharing such that no single party can access them
  alone, and defines a minimal, platform-agnostic core that any
  custodial service can adopt without seeking permission or paying a
  fee.
keywords:
  - digital-legacy
  - dead-mans-switch
  - shamir-secret-sharing
  - threshold-cryptography
  - estate-planning
  - cryptocurrency-inheritance
  - ed25519
  - quorum-based-verification
